    "body": "## Summary\n\nAffects `SimpleDiskCache.md5` in `app/src/main/java/com/idunnololz/summit/cache/SimpleDiskCache.kt`.\n\n`SimpleDiskCache` currently derives internal cache keys with MD5. The digest API does not accept MD5 when creating the digest, so the existing update and digest calls cannot follow its required call sequence.\n\nI renamed the helper to `sha256` and changed its sole caller to use it. The implementation keeps the existing UTF-8 conversion, update/digest flow, and exception handling while creating a SHA-256 digest instead. Internal cache-key values will change, but the code now uses an accepted digest algorithm.\n\nI found this while running the app under RVSec, a runtime-verification tool that watches the app's calls to the Java cryptography and TLS APIs and checks each sequence of calls against usage rules written in CrySL. `MessageDigestSpec` is the rule this code did not satisfy.\n\n## How was this tested?\n\n- No automated test was added in this change\n- [x] The patched module compiles successfully (`:app:compileDefaultDebugSources`); the full multi-module build was not completed in this environment\n\n---\n\n*I'm an undergraduate Computer Engineering student at the University of Brasília (UnB); this contribution is part of a research project on the analysis of Android apps, and I'm happy to adjust it to match the project's conventions.*",
